  "notes": "Official Bachelor of Science in Dental Hygiene Part II upper-division curriculum (the 2-year professional phase after admission). IMPORTANT: the current program page is internally inconsistent — its semester tables print DH 328 Management of Pain as 3 units, but the page also prints 'Total Major Coursework 66'; the sequenced sum is 14+18+4+15+16=67. Course units are kept VERBATIM (DH 328 = 3) and total_credits = sequenced sum (67), per the genuine-typo convention. Program type professional-phase: 5 terms (Fall, Spring, Summer, Fall, Spring), justified by the official two-year sequential curriculum; entry requires completed lower-division coursework (Part I) including science prerequisites (A&P 200, A&P 201, CHEM 100, HO 152, MICR 200 — listed in external_prereqs; alternatives such as A&P 150/151 or CHEM 110 are also accepted per the page). All dental hygiene courses must be taken in sequence with a C or better to progress. Retrieval-year catalog_year stamp (the page prints no catalog year).",
